From 9821f012ff27c8e2c4e3a1ed164ccca658cb64c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Jonat=C3=A3=20Bolzan=20Loss?= <jonata@jonata.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:15:50 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/24] Haiku: message pump on poll(), base/ OS calls, WebRTC,
 net

MessagePumpEpoll already keeps a poll() list beside its epoll set; Haiku,
which has no epoll or eventfd, always waits with poll() (epoll_haiku.h
gives the types and inert calls) and wakes through a pipe. base/:
random bytes from arc4random_buf (libbsd), stack bases and the debugger
check from get_thread_info/get_team_info, FILE_EXE from the app image,
no setproctitle, no sysctl, no syscall.h. WebRTC and the DNS address
sorter skip BSD headers Haiku lacks (sys/endian.h, in6_var.h).
